AUDIO
  SH N → SH IN
      the S&H samples its own noise, so every note draws a fresh voltage
  VCO SAW → VCF IN
  VCF LP → VCA IN
  VCA OUT → Audio 2 To "device output 1"
  VCA OUT → Audio 2 To "device output 2"

PITCH & GATE
  DUAL AD EOC → SH CLK
      each note's end-of-cycle clocks the next random value — the note chooses its successor
  DUAL AD EOC → DUAL AD TRIG
      end-of-cycle retriggers the envelope: the loop that makes the patch play itself
  DUAL ATT B OUT → VCO V/OCT

MODULATION
  SH OUT → DUAL ATT A IN
  DUAL ATT A OUT → DUAL AD TIME
      random voltage offset into the B channel's time input sets how long this note lasts
  DUAL AD ENV → MULT IN
      the envelope is both the loudness shape and the filter sweep, so short notes stay dark
  MULT 1 → VCA CV
  MULT 2 → VCF CV
